# G8 (text): the mouse in the file dialog's Save As. Places are cells: column, then row, row 0 being the menu bar. File > Save As... by
# menu clicks; a click on an entry selects it and puts its name in the field, a click on the Size header sorts, a double click on a folder
# goes in and on `..` goes back, the Look in drop-down and a place and Up change folder, a click in the File name field puts the caret
# there, the type drop-down picks a type, New folder makes its folder (the box takes keys only), Save with a name that is there asks and No
# keeps the dialog, a read-only file is refused and OK on the notice closes it, Cancel ends the dialog, and Yes saves.
@dialog
@dir QUILL
@place Quill C:\QUILL
@cwd C:\DOCS
@dir DOCS\LETTERS
@copy letter.qld DOCS\
@copy letter.rtf DOCS\
@copy plain.qld DOCS\
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.QLD 2026-11-24 18:45
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.RTF 2026-11-02 09:05
@stamp DOCS\PLAIN.QLD 2026-03-14 12:00
@readonly DOCS\PLAIN.QLD
@open C:\DOCS\LETTER.QLD
@click 3 0                    # File menu
@click 4 6                    # Save As...: the dialog
@click 20 7                   # PLAIN.QLD: selected, its name in the field
@click 36 3                   # the Size header: sorted by size
@dclick 20 5                  # LETTERS: opened
@dclick 20 4                  # .. : back in DOCS
@click 30 2                   # the Look in drop-down opens
@click 30 4                   # C:\
@click 8 8                    # the place Quill: C:\QUILL
@click 55 2                   # Up: C:\
@dclick 20 4                  # DOCS
@click 20 17                  # the File name field: the caret before the dot
@click 61 2                   # New folder: its box
@click 20 12                  # a click in the box does nothing
d r a f t s enter             # DRAFTS is made and selected
@click 54 17                  # the type drop-down opens
@click 60 14                  # Rich Text Format: LETTER.RTF is listed
@click 20 7                   # LETTER.RTF
@click 55 19                  # Save: it is there, so it asks
@click 41 12                  # No: back in the dialog
@click 67 19                  # Cancel: the dialog ends
@click 3 0
@click 4 6
@click 20 8                   # PLAIN.QLD
@click 55 19                  # Save: it is read-only
@click 38 12                  # OK
@click 67 19                  # Cancel
@click 3 0
@click 4 6
@click 54 17
@click 60 14
@click 20 7                   # LETTER.RTF
@click 55 19                  # Save: it asks
@click 31 12                  # Yes: saved
